---
import Post from "../../../layouts/Post.astro";
import NutritionNav from "../../../components/NutritionNav.astro";
const pages = import.meta.glob("../../../data/nutrition/investigations/*.md", { eager: true });
const entries = Object.entries(pages).map(([path, page]) => ({
  slug: path.split("/").pop().replace(/\.md$/, ""),
  ...page.frontmatter,
})).sort((a, b) => (a.order ?? 100) - (b.order ?? 100));
const categories = [
  ["foods", "Food choices", "Taste, portions and the evidence behind an optional food change."],
  ["dietary-patterns", "The whole eating pattern", "Questions about meals, hydration, storage and repeated observations."],
  ["recovery", "Training and recovery", "Enough food, connective tissue and performance supplements."],
  ["interactions", "Nutrients working together", "Protein and energy, bone loading, food absorption and laboratory interpretation."],
  ["experimental", "Experimental interventions", "Compound identity, exposure, human outcomes and unresolved tradeoffs."],
  ["methods", "How to read the evidence", "Intake references, measurements and the decisions they can support."],
];
const frontmatter = {
  title: "Nutrition investigations",
  description: "Research connecting foods, nutritional adequacy, training, recovery and experimental interventions.",
  updated: "2026-10-10",
};
---
<Post frontmatter={frontmatter}>
  <NutritionNav current="research" />
  <p>Some useful questions cross nutrient boundaries. These investigations follow foods and eating patterns, the demands of training, performance supplements, and newer experimental ideas. Each connects the relevant evidence to a practical decision and keeps the outcome being tested clear.</p>
  {entries.length > 0 ? categories.filter(([id]) => entries.some((entry) => entry.category === id)).map(([id, title, description]) => <section aria-labelledby={id}>
    <h2 id={id}>{title}</h2>
    <p>{description}</p>
    <ul>{entries.filter((entry) => entry.category === id).map((entry) => <li>
      <a href={`/nutrition/research/${entry.slug}/`}>{entry.title}</a>
      {entry.description && <span class="description">{entry.description}</span>}
    </li>)}</ul>
  </section>) : <p>Working research is being developed alongside the <a href="/nutrition/guide/">nutrient guide</a>.</p>}
  <h2>Reading an intervention</h2>
  <p>The relevant questions are what it changes, at what exposure, in which population, and with what demonstrated outcome. A result in cells, a change in a blood marker and an improvement in people's health or performance establish different things. The sections retain these distinctions beside their claims.</p>
  <p>The <a href="/nutrition-notebook/">notebook</a> holds the current decisions. The <a href="/nutrition/record/">food record</a> shows what I actually ate and how that felt.</p>
</Post>
<style>
  .description { display: block; color: var(--dim); font-size: 13px; margin-top: 4px; }
  li { margin-bottom: 20px; }
</style>
